{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"c2b0ea45ec7669e67326b49cc391778f42008cc8fbc7d4cc6c2b1c6432c27b9e","occurred_at":"2026-11-22T16:11:47Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[99,102]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-live-binding.py","quoted_text":"DEPENDENCY_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(?P<directive>Wants|Requires|Requisite|BindsTo|PartOf|Conflicts|\"\n    r\"WantedBy|RequiredBy|Also|Upholds|OnFailure|OnSuccess|Triggers|\"\n    r\"TriggersBy|Unit|Service)\\s*=\\s*(?P<value>.*)\")","reason":"The dependency scan’s DEPENDENCY_RE omits systemd’s stop-propagation directives. A unit using StopPropagatedFrom=crq-tick.service, or a crq unit using PropagatesStopTo=<co-tenant>, can propagate the fence stop to a co-tenant while discovery ignores it, defeating the intended protection. This is an ordinary correctness defect in the existing dependency scan, not a request for new scope.","target":"edde40371fb375fc7909891774c2a114db0599ef"},"finding_id":"c7b77c93896633be5163f44f39c7843bb564e25079db60acbfaa86176229b442","previous_event_id":"369c5f393833be477728c7608d6e410bec38f2edc21e9a02190d9e73d46649ac","review_id":"b08452801c153d71823e0063057ca8526a7754e9b9085e055e498d2c928878b1"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:c7b77c93896633be5163f44f39c7843bb564e25079db60acbfaa86176229b442:50fbdb7b5324c11486b523b0689b02251b65db044eb58ea795213ff8fe3d1f9b"}